Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects high-confidence technical zero events in single-cell RNA-seq
    data using SuperCell-style local memberships, low-rank reconstruction, and
    finite-sample empirical-Bayes zero-null testing with gene-wise false-discovery
    control. Recovery can retain the full SuperCell walktrap hierarchy and combine
    tree proximity with the original biological embedding so nearer positive donors
    contribute more strongly to query-specific expression baselines and local
    coexpression residual models. Predictive uncertainty is retained and observed
    non-dropout values are never overwritten.
